      "archived": false,
      "assetId": "000-064",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-16T19:10:47.71765359Z",
      "description": "Writing: The pen puts down a reliable line that's quite fine with just a hint of bounce. I had no problems with hard starts.\n\nFilling: Lever mechanism fills well and the lever has some tabs to keep it locked down.\n\nCondition: This one is a beauty! The body is shiny and the stripes have very impressive clarity and iridescence. The trim is in great shape as well, and there's an amber window in the section to check on your remaining ink level.\n\nIt took me a while to even figure out what this one is: a less-common lever-fill model made from the same Penline celluloid as Nozac pens, in approximately 1936. Mentally, I've taken to calling it a Conklin Yeszac. You take your fun where you can get it.\n\n\n",
